@page "/"
@using GSBC.Accounting.WASM.Features.Expenses
@inject DraftSession Session

<PageTitle>GSBC Finance Forms</PageTitle>

@*
    The landing page: the form, and the way back into anything already started.

    ONE CARD, not two. There are still two documents underneath and they still differ in almost every
    word, but which one a claimant needs is a question the form itself asks - and it asks it in terms of
    whose money was spent, which somebody who has just bought morning tea can answer without knowing
    what either document is called.

    The drafts card is second rather than first on purpose. Most people arriving here are starting a
    form, not resuming one, and a list they have no entries in would be the first thing they read.

    IT IS ALSO ABSENT ENTIRELY UNTIL THE BROWSER HAS A SESSION. Nothing on this client can read the
    __gsbc_anon cookie - it is HttpOnly - so DraftSession asks the server, and until it answers there is
    no honest way to offer somebody "your saved drafts": the link would lead to a list the server
    refuses to talk about. A first-time visitor sees the form and nothing else.
*@

<div class="layout norail">
    <main>
        <p class="lede">
            One form, and a person at the end of it. A submission here is <strong>not</strong> a
            ledger entry &mdash; it collects the claim, its receipts and its declarations so a
            reviewer can check them and file the result in Xero.
        </p>

        <section class="card">
            <header>
                <span class="num">01</span>
                <h3>Expense form</h3>
                <span class="hint">Reimbursement, or a church card purchase</span>
            </header>
            <div class="body">
                <p class="help">
                    For money you spent yourself and want back, or for a purchase already charged to a
                    church debit card. The first question asks which, and the rest of the form follows
                    from your answer. Either way it needs an itemised receipt behind every line.
                </p>
                @* cardlink is a mobile affordance and does nothing on a desktop width. A bare text
                   link is a ~20px tap target, and this is the only way into the form. *@
                <p><a class="cardlink" href="/forms/expense">Start an expense form</a></p>
            </div>
        </section>


        @if (Session.HasSession)
        {
            <section class="card">
                <header>
                    <span class="num">&mdash;</span>
                    <h3>Your saved drafts</h3>
                    <span class="hint">Kept for this browser</span>
                </header>
                <div class="body">
                    <p class="help">
                        The form saves itself as you fill it in, so you can close the page and come
                        back later. Drafts are kept for the browser you started them on &mdash; clearing
                        your cookies, or switching to another device, loses them &mdash; and a draft nobody
                        edits is deleted after 90 days.
                    </p>
                    <p><a class="cardlink" href="/drafts">See your saved drafts</a></p>
                </div>
            </section>
        }

        <p class="footnote">
            The form does not ask you to sign in, and it is not a substitute for approval. Sections 7
            and 8 &mdash; independent approval, and finance use &mdash; are completed after you submit,
            by somebody who is not you.
        </p>
    </main>
</div>

@code
{
    [CascadingParameter] private MainLayout Layout { get; set; } = default!;

    protected override void OnInitialized() => Layout.SetTitle("Finance Forms");

    // The card appears on the second render, once the server has said whether this browser owns
    // anything. Deliberately silent on failure: this page has nothing to tell somebody about drafts if
    // it cannot find out, and a banner here would be about the plumbing rather than about their form.
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            await Session.DraftsAsync();
        }
        catch
        {
            // Unreachable server. Leaves the card hidden, which is the same answer as no session.
        }
    }

}
